sedalion.text:
Today the Church rejoiceth, singeth and adorneth herself, celebrating the forefeast of the nativity;
for it is truly an all-holy solemnity,
and she doth therefore array herself for the Lord of glory,
and we all cry out to Christ God://
O Lover of mankind, have mercy upon us who hymn Thee!

ode7.irmos:
In Babylon the Children feared not the fiery furnace;
but cast into the midst of the flames they were bedewed and sang:
'O Lord God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou.'

